01:07:58.721 --> 01:08:00.390
I was working in public goods,

01:08:00.391 --> 01:08:03.180
and then actually
the US military asked me to work

01:08:03.181 --> 01:08:04.890
on cultural variations so

01:08:04.891 --> 01:08:06.240
I put these two things together.

01:08:06.241 --> 01:08:07.700
It turns out that
different people

01:08:07.701 --> 01:08:09.190
treat people that
invest in the public.

01:08:09.191 --> 01:08:11.570
Different regions
of the world have

01:08:11.571 --> 01:08:13.200
people who tend to treat

01:08:13.201 --> 01:08:15.460
people differently than
invest in the public good,

01:08:15.461 --> 01:08:18.080
and some of them
actually punish those

01:08:18.081 --> 01:08:21.480
who give more than they
do to the public good.

01:08:21.481 --> 01:08:23.420
If they're allowed to
because this is all

01:08:23.421 --> 01:08:25.240
secret like
a rat lab experiments.

01:08:25.241 --> 01:08:26.450
So, if they could
figure out the sneaky

01:08:26.451 --> 01:08:27.640
way like vandalism or

01:08:27.641 --> 01:08:29.600
something to punish the people

01:08:29.601 --> 01:08:30.640
who have been giving
to the public good,

01:08:30.641 --> 01:08:33.520
they will and actually
have more tendency to do

01:08:33.521 --> 01:08:37.350
that in places that have
lower rule of law and lower GDP,

01:08:37.351 --> 01:08:39.945
and unfortunately those are
two correlated things, too.

01:08:39.946 --> 01:08:42.680
The economy is always
complicated like that.

01:08:42.681 --> 01:08:48.935
So, the point is that you have
to take care of yourself.

01:08:48.936 --> 01:08:51.300
There's actually an expression
in Eastern Europe in

01:08:51.301 --> 01:08:53.700
Slavic languages that
if you don't steal,

01:08:53.701 --> 01:08:55.060
you steal from your family.

01:08:55.061 --> 01:09:01.845
So, there's a baseline

01:09:01.846 --> 01:09:03.930
of making sure that
you stay alive

01:09:03.931 --> 01:09:06.180
and that you need to be able
to do individual investment.

01:09:06.181 --> 01:09:09.150
So, I think part of what
society tends to do is

01:09:09.151 --> 01:09:10.320
try to get you to invest in

01:09:10.321 --> 01:09:12.400
society and so our culture
tends to do that,

01:09:12.401 --> 01:09:14.370
and so it's probably
slightly overshooting

01:09:14.371 --> 01:09:15.720
the level at which you should

01:09:15.721 --> 01:09:17.345
be investing in the social level.

01:09:17.346 --> 01:09:19.890
So to give an immediate
example in AI,

01:09:19.891 --> 01:09:22.040
when Google had
their driverless cars

01:09:22.041 --> 01:09:23.670
going around in Mountain View,

01:09:23.671 --> 01:09:25.780
they had the strict rules

01:09:25.781 --> 01:09:27.090
of the road about what
you're supposed to do at

01:09:27.091 --> 01:09:28.620
a four-way stop and

01:09:28.621 --> 01:09:30.560
the Google cars were
never going to go,

01:09:30.561 --> 01:09:33.380
and they had to build into
it what people always do,

01:09:33.381 --> 01:09:35.680
which is that at some point
you take the initiative,

01:09:35.681 --> 01:09:37.080
you don't wait till
every other car

01:09:37.081 --> 01:09:38.755
has come to a full stop
and then go.

01:09:38.756 --> 01:09:39.990
You have to say, "Okay, I've

01:09:39.991 --> 01:09:41.500
been here long enough,"
and start going.

01:09:41.501 --> 01:09:46.780
I don't think we

01:09:46.781 --> 01:09:49.220
necessarily have to
build our AI up to

01:09:49.221 --> 01:09:52.455
the paragon of ideal morality,

01:09:52.456 --> 01:09:55.040
but I do think we
need to, in fact,

01:09:55.041 --> 01:09:56.390
I think you necessarily have

01:09:56.391 --> 01:09:59.120
to equilibrate that
a little bit more.

01:09:59.121 --> 01:10:01.140
That's one of the weird
interesting things that

01:10:01.141 --> 01:10:03.140
all this is going to bring
up. We actually are.

01:10:03.141 --> 01:10:04.690
This interacts badly,

01:10:04.691 --> 01:10:08.190
accountability interacts
badly with privacy,

01:10:08.191 --> 01:10:10.665
but I think it's
a fixable problem.

01:10:10.666 --> 01:10:12.630
I'm just saying that it was
something we have to defend,

01:10:12.631 --> 01:10:14.280
but I think we are going
to become much more

01:10:14.281 --> 01:10:16.350
explicitly aware of
a lot of the things we

01:10:16.351 --> 01:10:18.290
had previously not been aware

01:10:18.291 --> 01:10:20.480
of because again explicitly
we were doing things,

01:10:20.481 --> 01:10:21.470
we're being encouraged to do

01:10:21.471 --> 01:10:22.660
things where in some sets are

01:10:22.661 --> 01:10:25.650
natural but turned out
to be good and useful.

01:10:25.651 --> 01:10:27.400
Does that answer the question?

01:10:27.401 --> 01:10:29.570
&gt;&gt; Yeah, and I actually
have a follow-up question

01:10:29.571 --> 01:10:31.280
which is that kind of

01:10:31.281 --> 01:10:32.540
assumes that there is

01:10:32.541 --> 01:10:36.425
a common understanding of
what socially good is.

01:10:36.426 --> 01:10:39.290
I'm sure you thought about

01:10:39.291 --> 01:10:42.650
there could be cases
where a solution could

01:10:42.651 --> 01:10:44.570
be better for the majority

01:10:44.571 --> 01:10:47.240
and there could be
another solution

01:10:47.241 --> 01:10:49.280
that is worse for
the majority but

01:10:49.281 --> 01:10:52.325
definitely significantly
better for the minority,

01:10:52.326 --> 01:10:54.200
and this is really
real with all of

01:10:54.201 --> 01:10:56.870
the perceptive systems
where people talk about

01:10:56.871 --> 01:10:59.360
trading off percentage
they can receive

01:10:59.361 --> 01:11:02.300
for something in
return and so forth.

01:11:02.301 --> 01:11:04.460
&gt;&gt; Yeah. What this
means and this is,

01:11:04.461 --> 01:11:05.660
I actually wrote a paper
about this while I

01:11:05.661 --> 01:11:07.860
was still a PhD student too,

01:11:07.861 --> 01:11:11.790
that the closer AI gets
to human intelligence,

01:11:11.791 --> 01:11:13.750
the more what we're
talking about it.

01:11:13.751 --> 01:11:15.000
That is fundamentally what

01:11:15.001 --> 01:11:16.370
political scientists talk about

01:11:16.371 --> 01:11:17.430
when they talk about democracy,

01:11:17.431 --> 01:11:19.780
defending the rights
of the minority.

01:11:21.040 --> 01:11:23.230
Half of us dropped out of

01:11:23.231 --> 01:11:25.570
undergraduate or whatever
and blindly go and just

01:11:25.571 --> 01:11:27.080
do a lot of programming
and not realizing

01:11:27.081 --> 01:11:29.685
these entire disciplines are
working on these problems.

01:11:29.686 --> 01:11:32.045
So now, we are society.

01:11:32.046 --> 01:11:34.075
We have to deal with
all those problems,

01:11:34.076 --> 01:11:37.460
the defending the rights of
the minority and the fact

01:11:37.461 --> 01:11:41.350
that there isn't a particular
absolute correct solution.

01:11:41.351 --> 01:11:43.615
That solutions may be different
in different contexts.

01:11:43.616 --> 01:11:45.860
That's the kind of
complexities that law

01:11:45.861 --> 01:11:49.635
and politics have had to
deal with for a millennia.

01:11:49.636 --> 01:11:51.310
Yeah, absolutely.

01:11:51.311 --> 01:11:55.220
&gt;&gt; It's an ambiguous question
but bear with me.

01:11:55.221 --> 01:11:56.330
&gt;&gt; That's all right.

01:11:56.331 --> 01:11:58.190
&gt;&gt; Should or could

01:11:58.191 --> 01:12:03.095
a moral agent is such without
being part of a society?

01:12:03.096 --> 01:12:04.650
How can we be a moral agent

01:12:04.651 --> 01:12:06.170
without being part
of that society?

01:12:06.171 --> 01:12:06.740
&gt;&gt; Okay.

01:12:06.741 --> 01:12:08.780
&gt;&gt; Or should you?

01:12:08.781 --> 01:12:10.230
&gt;&gt; Right. First of
all, we need to

01:12:10.231 --> 01:12:11.715
disconfirm these two terms.

01:12:11.716 --> 01:12:15.125
So, there's an agent being
moral taking us moral actions,

01:12:15.126 --> 01:12:17.330
and there's the moral agent,
as I just described,

01:12:17.331 --> 01:12:18.490
which is the thing
that's being held

01:12:18.491 --> 01:12:20.145
accountable for its actions.

01:12:20.146 --> 01:12:23.665
&gt;&gt; Then backtracking, can
you be a moral agent?

01:12:23.666 --> 01:12:25.030
&gt;&gt; I don't think, for either

01:12:25.031 --> 01:12:26.400
of those two
definitions actually,

01:12:26.401 --> 01:12:27.980
you can be without in society

01:12:27.981 --> 01:12:29.250
because the society is one that's

01:12:29.251 --> 01:12:30.590
declaring the rules
that the person

01:12:30.591 --> 01:12:32.835
being moral is following,

01:12:32.836 --> 01:12:35.950
and for the moral agent

01:12:35.951 --> 01:12:38.330
that's been defined
by the society,

01:12:38.331 --> 01:12:39.900
it's basically the side of

01:12:39.901 --> 01:12:41.590
responsible actors
where obviously

01:12:41.591 --> 01:12:42.810
the society what defines it.

01:12:42.811 --> 01:12:43.840
So for both of those,

01:12:43.841 --> 01:12:45.260
I think you need a society to get

01:12:45.261 --> 01:12:47.000
the definitions for the morality.

01:12:47.001 --> 01:12:49.890
I don't think that morality
exist in a vacuum,

01:12:49.891 --> 01:12:51.560
but that's okay
because you're not

01:12:51.561 --> 01:12:53.230
going to get intelligence
in a vacuum either.

01:12:53.231 --> 01:12:56.550
The microbial will
totally take it out.

01:12:58.120 --> 01:13:01.955
All of us are intelligent
cognitive species.

01:13:01.956 --> 01:13:04.850
We all have a social.

01:13:04.851 --> 01:13:06.340
If nothing else, we
come from parents.

01:13:06.341 --> 01:13:09.470
We're all the products
of sexual reproduction.

01:13:09.471 --> 01:13:17.310
So, yeah.

01:13:17.311 --> 01:13:19.840
&gt;&gt; I'm really curious
about your last piece,

01:13:19.841 --> 01:13:22.040
about how to control
that third threat,

01:13:22.041 --> 01:13:25.635
I'm just like malicious AI
and specifically regulation.

01:13:25.636 --> 01:13:26.950
So, what are some of

01:13:26.951 --> 01:13:28.250
the government regulations that

01:13:28.251 --> 01:13:29.510
you foresee and what would you

01:13:29.511 --> 01:13:32.400
recommend for those of us
in the technical community

01:13:32.401 --> 01:13:35.500
to stay up-to-date on
those and get to that

01:13:35.501 --> 01:13:36.960
&gt;&gt; Well, the main thing
that we're trying to do

01:13:36.961 --> 01:13:38.380
in the UK at least
which is one of

01:13:38.381 --> 01:13:41.700
the most- I've been in
academics since 2002.

01:13:41.701 --> 01:13:44.130
So, I've been an adult
since I don't know when,

01:13:44.131 --> 01:13:46.070
but basically I've
been a professional in

01:13:46.071 --> 01:13:48.070
this particular
discipline since 2002,

01:13:48.071 --> 01:13:52.050
so I'm just more
familiar in Britain.

01:13:52.051 --> 01:13:54.135
But at least in Britain,

01:13:54.136 --> 01:13:57.370
we don't feel like we
need a lot of new laws.

01:13:57.371 --> 01:13:58.850
We just need to
start applying them

01:13:58.851 --> 01:14:01.675
into ICT and into software,

01:14:01.676 --> 01:14:02.920
which is something
we hadn't been doing

01:14:02.921 --> 01:14:04.950
before because people
didn't understand it.

01:14:04.951 --> 01:14:07.520
So, I think the
main thing is if we

01:14:07.521 --> 01:14:10.390
maintain the current standards
of accountability,

01:14:10.391 --> 01:14:13.155
then that will encourage-
so if I just say we.

01:14:13.156 --> 01:14:17.530
If the government, which I
do feel we're all part of,

01:14:17.531 --> 01:14:22.290
if the government part
of us maintains

01:14:22.291 --> 01:14:26.230
accountability into
the software industry

01:14:26.231 --> 01:14:27.500
and starts understanding it,

01:14:27.501 --> 01:14:29.200
and actually McCrock had

01:14:29.201 --> 01:14:33.420
a great interviewing
Wyatt about this.

01:14:33.421 --> 01:14:35.020
Of course we're always watching

01:14:35.021 --> 01:14:36.190
new industry for a while for

01:14:36.191 --> 01:14:38.790
a few decades and then we
get involved. But anyway.

01:14:38.791 --> 01:14:41.090
So, if they start
pursuing accountability,

01:14:41.091 --> 01:14:43.040
then we, the other part of we,

01:14:43.041 --> 01:14:45.140
the software industry,
are going to be highly

01:14:45.141 --> 01:14:47.810
motivated to be able
to have transparency.

01:14:47.811 --> 01:14:49.610
At least sufficient transparency

01:14:49.611 --> 01:14:51.785
so that we can prove that
we've done due diligence.

01:14:51.786 --> 01:14:53.560
Right? So, because you're

01:14:53.561 --> 01:14:54.970
not going to have
perfect transparency.

01:14:54.971 --> 01:14:56.215
I already said this
to one of you.

01:14:56.216 --> 01:14:58.060
I think it was you, today.

01:14:58.061 --> 01:15:00.770
But there's this thing called the

01:15:00.771 --> 01:15:03.510
map of Germany problem and
I've no idea why it's Germany.

01:15:03.511 --> 01:15:06.350
But the point is that a map
of Germany that was perfect,

01:15:06.351 --> 01:15:07.640
that had every detail,

01:15:07.641 --> 01:15:10.575
would be the same size as
Germany and it would be no use.

01:15:10.576 --> 01:15:12.890
This is actually
another re-framing of

01:15:12.891 --> 01:15:14.650
the whole box thing
about all models

01:15:14.651 --> 01:15:17.270
are rhymed but some
are useful, right?

01:15:17.271 --> 01:15:21.300
So, there is of

01:15:21.301 --> 01:15:22.330
course a trade-off about how

01:15:22.331 --> 01:15:23.370
much transparency you can have,

01:15:23.371 --> 01:15:24.470
how much explainability you can

01:15:24.471 --> 01:15:26.225
have, those kinds of things.

01:15:26.226 --> 01:15:28.290
But we can motivate

01:15:28.291 --> 01:15:30.160
companies to make the
trade-off themselves

01:15:30.161 --> 01:15:31.850
internally rather than
mandating the amount of

01:15:31.851 --> 01:15:35.170
transparency by just
maintaining accountability,

01:15:35.171 --> 01:15:37.320
and accountability is
actually already in the law.

01:15:37.321 --> 01:15:38.885
It just hasn't been pursued

01:15:38.886 --> 01:15:40.780
into the technology
companies before,

01:15:40.781 --> 01:15:42.270
and now the governments are

01:15:42.271 --> 01:15:44.240
realizing technology
companies matter.

01:15:44.241 --> 01:15:46.500
So, maybe they will
just start pursuing it.

01:15:46.501 --> 01:15:49.065
So, what we're trying
to say is that

01:15:49.066 --> 01:15:53.015
we don't really need
so much new laws and so

01:15:53.016 --> 01:15:54.650
we need new practice and

01:15:54.651 --> 01:16:00.720
just better education in
the prosecutor's offices.

01:16:04.540 --> 01:16:07.130
Actually, again,
talking to the people,

01:16:07.131 --> 01:16:08.410
I've only talked to
three people so far,

01:16:08.411 --> 01:16:09.695
I don't crap up names but it

01:16:09.696 --> 01:16:11.630
sounds like Microsoft is already

01:16:11.631 --> 01:16:16.950
realizing this is
a big corporate entity.

01:16:16.951 --> 01:16:18.880
You can cast in the positive way,

01:16:18.881 --> 01:16:20.650
which is that you
want the software

01:16:20.651 --> 01:16:22.735
to be doing what's
best for society.

01:16:22.736 --> 01:16:24.660
You can also say that
you want to avoid

01:16:24.661 --> 01:16:28.040
big corporate
liability cost, right?

01:16:28.041 --> 01:16:29.930
Those come for free together.

01:16:29.931 --> 01:16:33.805
&gt;&gt; I have a question,

01:16:33.806 --> 01:16:35.750
there's this interesting- let's

01:16:35.751 --> 01:16:37.620
quote the [inaudible] I
like to hear your thoughts.

01:16:37.621 --> 01:16:40.270
Does the opinion or the school
of thought that says,

01:16:40.271 --> 01:16:42.140
"Let's create Artificial
Intelligence"

01:16:42.141 --> 01:16:43.950
and the school of
thought that says,

01:16:43.951 --> 01:16:45.390
"No, that's fool's errand let's

01:16:45.391 --> 01:16:48.290
create assist of intelligence."

01:16:48.291 --> 01:16:51.210
Something that is always
partnering with a human,

01:16:51.211 --> 01:16:53.950
cannot have
independent behaviors,

01:16:53.951 --> 01:16:55.830
it's always at the service of

01:16:55.831 --> 01:16:59.175
[inaudible] prosthesis
if you may of a human.

01:16:59.176 --> 01:17:03.210
What do you think things should
go if you have a choice?

01:17:03.211 --> 01:17:06.105
&gt;&gt; Okay. So, I think

01:17:06.106 --> 01:17:10.030
that that's a great question,
I'm glad you asked it.

01:17:10.400 --> 01:17:12.720
You're not quite
using the language

01:17:12.721 --> 01:17:14.665
I presented here but that's okay.

01:17:14.666 --> 01:17:17.620
Because you're using for
Artificial Intelligence,

01:17:17.621 --> 01:17:19.040
so I briefly mentioned
a lot of people are

01:17:19.041 --> 01:17:21.015
using for Artificial
General Intelligence.

01:17:21.016 --> 01:17:22.390
By which they mean all kinds of

01:17:22.391 --> 01:17:24.720
contradictory things because
it's not a coherent thing,

01:17:24.721 --> 01:17:27.780
and I was mostly talking
about the omniscient AGI.

01:17:27.781 --> 01:17:29.965
But you're talking about
the human-like AGI,

01:17:29.966 --> 01:17:31.660
that there's something
that's really is human

01:17:31.661 --> 01:17:33.735
unconscious and all those
other kinds of things.

01:17:33.736 --> 01:17:39.180
So, a lot of

01:17:39.181 --> 01:17:41.340
this was about that and
it didn't come together,

01:17:41.341 --> 01:17:42.130
so now I have a chance to

01:17:42.131 --> 01:17:43.180
bring it together,
so that's great.

01:17:43.181 --> 01:17:44.855
Thank you very much
for your question.

01:17:44.856 --> 01:17:51.020
The point is that we can't
create something out of

01:17:51.021 --> 01:17:54.110
silicone that is an agent in

01:17:54.111 --> 01:17:58.890
our society as it's
currently run.

01:17:58.891 --> 01:18:02.985
Because the sanctions that
we do to keep each other

01:18:02.986 --> 01:18:04.545
from doing the wrong things

01:18:04.546 --> 01:18:06.710
aren't going to
work on a machine.

01:18:06.711 --> 01:18:09.750
Right? Machines are not
going to have- I mean,

01:18:09.751 --> 01:18:12.105
you could build into a robot

01:18:12.106 --> 01:18:15.060
a bomb and a timer and the timer

01:18:15.061 --> 01:18:17.620
is set when there's
no other person in the room and

01:18:17.621 --> 01:18:18.950
the bomb is going to
go off if there's

01:18:18.951 --> 01:18:20.465
no person around
for five minutes.

01:18:20.466 --> 01:18:21.720
Okay. You can say, well that's

01:18:21.721 --> 01:18:23.100
kind of like humans
that they don't like to

01:18:23.101 --> 01:18:25.275
be isolated because- but it's

01:18:25.276 --> 01:18:26.500
not liking to be

01:18:26.501 --> 01:18:28.470
isolated to know that you're
just going to blow up.

01:18:28.471 --> 01:18:31.230
Right? Watch your investment
not being blown up.

01:18:31.231 --> 01:18:33.120
In humans and in fish
and everything else,

01:18:33.121 --> 01:18:34.765
there's a systemic stress.

01:18:34.766 --> 01:18:36.850
Right? If we have

01:18:36.851 --> 01:18:39.060
well-designed AI that we can

01:18:39.061 --> 01:18:41.510
be responsible and accountable
for and all those things,

01:18:41.511 --> 01:18:43.660
you're going to have things
like systemic stress.

01:18:43.661 --> 01:18:44.000
You are going to have

01:18:44.001 --> 01:18:45.500
modularity and you're
going to have ways of

01:18:45.501 --> 01:18:47.625
knowing it's going to
be more separable.

01:18:47.626 --> 01:18:49.110
So, I don't think there's

01:18:49.111 --> 01:18:53.010
a safe way to build
a system- basically,

01:18:53.011 --> 01:18:54.780
I think there's no way that
we can build a system that we

01:18:54.781 --> 01:18:56.680
